## API Gateway

All client requests should be sent through:

```text
http://localhost:8765
```

The API Gateway routes requests to services registered with Eureka.

```text
/api/users/**          → user-service
/api/orders/**         → order-service
/api/payments/**       → payment-service
/api/notifications/**  → notification-service
```

## API Overview

### Users

```http
POST /api/users/register
POST /api/users/login
GET  /api/users/getUser
```

### Orders

```http
POST  /api/orders
GET   /api/orders
GET   /api/orders/{orderId}
PATCH /api/orders/{orderId}/status
POST  /api/orders/{orderId}/cancel
```

### Payments

```http
POST  /api/payments
GET   /api/payments/{paymentId}
GET   /api/payments/order/{orderId}
PATCH /api/payments/{paymentId}/status
```

### Notifications

```http
POST /api/notifications
GET  /api/notifications
GET  /api/notifications/{notificationId}
POST /api/notifications/{notificationId}/markAsRead
POST /api/notifications/markAllAsRead
```

## Docker Services

Docker Compose starts the following containers:

```text
api-gateway
spring-cloud-config-server
naming-server
user-service
order-service
payment-service
notification-service
user-db
order-db
payment-db
notification-db
rabbitmq
```

## Local Ports

```text
API Gateway:          http://localhost:8765
Eureka Dashboard:     http://localhost:8761
Config Server:        http://localhost:8888

user-service:         http://localhost:8084
order-service:        http://localhost:8081
payment-service:      http://localhost:8082
notification-service: http://localhost:8083

user-db:              localhost:3311
order-db:             localhost:3308
payment-db:           localhost:3309
notification-db:      localhost:3310

RabbitMQ Broker:      localhost:5672
RabbitMQ UI:          http://localhost:15672
```

RabbitMQ default login:

```text
username: guest
password: guest
```

## Running the Project

From the root directory, build and start the complete application:

```bash
docker compose build --no-cache
docker compose up -d
```

Verify that all containers are running:

```bash
docker compose ps
```

View logs:

```bash
docker compose logs -f
```

Stop the application:

```bash
docker compose down
```

## Sample User Registration

```http
POST http://localhost:8765/api/users/register
Content-Type: application/json
```

```json
{
  "name": "Maggie Lorena",
  "email": "MaggieLorena@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "role": "CUSTOMER"
}
```

## Sample Login Request

```http
POST http://localhost:8765/api/users/login
Content-Type: application/json
```

```json
{
  "email": "MaggieLorena@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}
```

The login endpoint returns a JWT that must be included when calling protected endpoints.

## Sample Order Request

```http
POST http://localhost:8765/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer <JWT_TOKEN>
Content-Type: application/json
```

```json
{
  "customerName": "Maggie Lorena",
  "customerEmail": "MaggieLorena@example.com",
  "customerPhone": "6145551001",
  "items": [
    {
      "productName": "Laptop Stand",
      "quantity": 1,
      "price": 59.99
    },
    {
      "productName": "Wireless Keyboard",
      "quantity": 1,
      "price": 79.99
    }
  ]
}
```

Example initial order response:

```json
{
  "id": 3,
  "customerName": "Maggie Lorena",
  "customerEmail": "MaggieLorena@example.com",
  "customerPhone": "6145551001",
  "total": 139.98,
  "status": "PENDING"
}
```

After payment processing, the final order status becomes:

```text
CONFIRMED
```

or:

```text
PAYMENT_FAILED
```

## Current Version

This is V2 of the Order Processing Microservices project.

V2 expands the original event-driven application by adding:

* User management
* JWT authentication
* API Gateway routing
* Eureka service discovery
* Spring Cloud Config
* Centralized application entry point
* Authenticated requests across services
* Complete Docker Compose orchestration

The core V2 system has been implemented and tested successfully from user registration through order creation, payment processing, order status updates, and notification generation.

